02_Operators.md
<br>
Operator: A symbol that tells the program to perform an action on values or variables
examples:
+ → adds numbers
- → subtracts
* → multiplies
/ → divides
== → checks if two values are equal
> → checks if one value is greater than another
<br>
2. Key C# Syntax
<br>
int a = 10;
int b = 5;

int sum = a + b;        // addition
int diff = a - b;       // subtraction
bool isEqual = (a == b); // comparison
<br>
+, -, *, / = arithmetic operators
==, !=, >, < = comparison operators
operands = the values being used (a, b)
result = the value after the operation
